{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqsem2307jf","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Agentic search context delivery clip fixed by full content field","summary":"Root cause of our-way-prod arm scoring 0/5 on LongMemEval Oracle (answered \"I don't know\" despite grader firing and keeping the right chunk): the context delivered to the answerer was clipped to the 200-char display summary BEFORE reaching context_deps. memory-search.js sets result.summary via slice(0,200); rankResults runs every result through compactResult which DROPS all unlisted fields and reclips to 240; contextDependencyFromResult then emits summary.slice(0,240) (a no-op since it was already <=200). Source chunks (lib/note-source-cluster.js CHUNK_CHARS=1200) store the full answer-bearing text in node.summary, so 200 chars dropped ~83% of the chunk and truncated the answer (e.g. GPS-system text on the \"first issue with my new car\" probe). Fix (token-aware, agentic-path-only): searchUrlForPlan sets full_content=1 (only the subconscious agentic paths build that URL; one-shot GET /search never sets it). compileSearchContext on that flag attaches a bounded content field (<=1200, the source-chunk granularity) from the live node text, leaving the 200-char display summary untouched. compactResult preserves content (bounded). contextDependencyFromResult emits content as the delivered summary when present, else the prior 240 clip. Item count already bounded (<=5 context_deps) so worst-case ~5x1200 chars. Bench gotcha discovered: bench _find_daemon_js prefers a daemon.js whose sibling node_modules/@xenova exists; a git worktree has no node_modules, so it fell back to the MAIN repo daemon.js and would NOT exercise a worktree lib fix. Fix: create a node_modules junction in the worktree to the main repo node_modules so the worktree daemon.js wins resolution.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-24T18:25:47.532Z","vec":[-0.06042442470788956,0.0182062815874815,-0.01533208042383194,0.022